# DET-002 – Encoded PowerShell

## Purpose
Detect potential use of Base64-encoded PowerShell commands.

## MITRE ATT&CK
T1059.001 – Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell

## Data Source
- Sysmon Event ID 1

## SPL

```spl
index=sysmon host=WIN11-01 powershell.exe
("-enc" OR "-encodedcommand")
```

## Why this matters

Attackers frequently use encoded PowerShell to hide malicious commands from defenders.

## False Positives

- Administrative automation
- Legitimate software deployment
- Enterprise management tools

## Test Performed

No encoded PowerShell executed during this sprint.

Detection validated syntactically.

## Future Improvements

- Alert only when parent process is Office or Explorer.
- Exclude known administrative scripts.
